{"title":"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">1999 CEMC Pascal #12</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">1999 CEMC Cayley #11</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">1999 CEMC Fermat #8</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The time on a digital clock is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/09880453ab8ac423ff611947078c727f4c8dba62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5:55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. How many minutes will pass before the clock next shows a time with all digits identical?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61ccd55c30d548e1f734c3013143568bc178cc82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 71 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 72 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 255 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 316 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 436$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"461\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can't be used because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes in an hour. This means that the next time must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/4256515d81ae8345a9517f1e51aa66021d211fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11:11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The time that passes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/09880453ab8ac423ff611947078c727f4c8dba62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5:55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b7575810ecaa5f0b23bfc1d16dfda726c668fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11:00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes long, so the time that passes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/09880453ab8ac423ff611947078c727f4c8dba62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5:55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/4256515d81ae8345a9517f1e51aa66021d211fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11:11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/1395ff2711f131beb3c97b56e181c174fe68f800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 11 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> minutes long.\n</p><p>Converting this time into minutes, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbf7034e256e989d248269470c4890fbc5b77b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 60 + 16 = 300 + 16 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 316}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"282\" height=\"30\" /> minutes will pass.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal\">1999 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b